# Hygiene is by choice (MC30): a name a macro writes stays as written,
# so x:t_hree< binds x around its text and the text's x is that one;
# x:t_wice< asks []G_ENSYM for a fresh name, so a t of your own is yours.
== SOURCE
"x:" u_se< "Macros"
x := 10
@ x:t_hree< "x + 1"
t := 5
@ x:t_wice< "t + 1"
== EXPAND
"x:" u_se< "Macros"
x := 10
{ @ -> x := 3; x + 1 } @
t := 5
{ @ -> g1:t := 2; g1:t * (t + 1) } @
== RESULT
4
12
